  "hotFileRule": "A lane edits a hot file only to delete the declarations listed under its monolithDeletions, or within the JSON key paths its hotFileGrants lists for that file (\"*\" grants the whole file). A lane whose owns lists a hot file's exact path writes that file freely. Any other hot-file edit goes through the integration lane.",
  "ownershipRule": "A lane owns its owns globs plus every legacy file LEGACY_TERRITORY in lint/context-map.ts assigns to a context in its territory. contractFiles are the exception: only lane 0 writes them.",
  "callerMoveGrant": "A lane that deletes a declaration from a legacy file may edit any file outside src/ only to repoint imports and call sites of that declaration to its new owner, in the same slice as the deletion.",
  "contractRule": "Lane 0 owns only what crosses an arrow: the published domain types and boundary ports in contractFiles. Each lane owns the rest of its context, including its own application layer and adapters. A lane that needs a cross-arrow change asks lane 0 for it, naming the design move it needs.",
